# Licensing

Welcome to the Codexeron Licensing Documentation.

This section provides general information about product licenses on the Codexeron Marketplace.

Licenses define how purchased digital products can be used and help protect both buyers and sellers.

---

# License Overview

When a buyer purchases a product, a license may define:

- Product ownership
- Usage permissions
- Access rights
- Usage limitations
- Update availability

---

# License Purpose

Licensing helps:

- Protect developer work.
- Provide clear usage rules.
- Prevent unauthorized distribution.
- Create a trusted marketplace environment.

---

# License Information

A license may include:

- License ID
- Product information
- Purchase information
- License type
- Status
- Usage conditions

---

# License Types

Available license models may vary depending on product requirements.

Examples:

- Single Project License
- Multiple Project License
- Extended License
- Custom License

---

# Buyer Responsibilities

Buyers should:

- Review license terms before purchase.
- Use products according to permissions.
- Protect purchased files.
- Avoid unauthorized sharing or redistribution.

---

# Seller Responsibilities

Sellers should:

- Provide clear license information.
- Define product usage conditions.
- Respect buyer purchase rights.
- Keep license information accurate.

---

# License Security

Codexeron may provide license-related security features such as:

- License validation
- Ownership verification
- Access control
- Product protection mechanisms

---

# Learn More

For detailed license information and policies, visit:

https://www.codexeron.com

